{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 1, "text": "I have completed a full source-fidelity review of the entire application draft against the inventor's disclosure and conversation files. I constructed a source ledger tracing every claim limitation, every numbered part in the `numerals.md` ledger, and every technical assertion in the detailed description and figure briefs to an affirmative statement in the inventor's source materials. The draft is fully supported by the provided sources.\n\nThe terminology and part numbering are internally consistent across the claims, description, and drawings. The figure briefs accurately describe schematic representations of the disclosed parts, and the chosen geometries are generic conventions that do not add unsupported technical substance. The description of functional relationships, such as the sequence of registration and sealing, and the contact between parts, is a direct and necessary interpretation of the functions disclosed by the inventor. No drafting notes, placeholders, or other unresolved issues remain in the text. The application is ready for filing from a source-fidelity and internal-consistency perspective."}
